            <ArticleTitle>Intravenous phentolamine mesylate alleviates the pain of pancreatic carcinoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>263-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case report describes the successful alleviation of the pain of pancreatic carcinoma with intravenous phentolamine mesylate. A 2 day infusion gave relief for 26 days on the first occasion and for 12 weeks after the second infusion. The possible mode of action is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
